Z||000081||Galen||07-29-2001||03:14 AM||||I personally find FieroBaby's posts to be far less offensive than many of mine have been. I find however my offensiveness is projected in a far less subtle and easier to notice way. In that sense maybe FieroBaby is more offensive. But in my own personal opinion, I highly doubt it.<P>Santa, I personally do not care if that is or is not your girlfriend, or perhaps I do otherwise I would not be posting this here. What I do care about is what has been promised to me that you would do. And I have yet to receive.<P>And to the rest of you, a subtle bit of offensiveness. Doooobeeedooobeeedope!<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple">"And God said there shall be one in thy owns image, and he made me"</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/download.html" TARGET=_blank>Download FieroProject.com Chat Client v1.50 Today</A>||||reg||1
Z||000082||Songman||07-29-2001||02:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Stage-2GT:<BR><B> Songman, your cool dude and you have a very chivalrous attitude. I can respect that. But remember not every damsel in distress really wants to be rescued.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I appreciate your respect for my attitude, and I respect yours as well. And that is all I ever ask for here, whether it be male or female. If you go look at the chronology of my posts yesterday, you'll see that before I made my statements in response to the attack on Fierobaby, I made statements about the guy saying his girlfriend called the guy a geek. So I don't just defend women, I defend anyone who is attacked.<P>I'm not mad at anyone, and even if I get upset it goes away quickly. I want to be friends with everyone here. I had to leave yesterday and didn't get to post the rest of my feelings on this subject.<P>I guess the reason I am the way I am is because I grew up with an abusive step-father who belittled me all of my life. I went to school and had absolutely no self-respect. I was a geek. The smart kid in class that people were nice to so he would do their homework for them. I never felt like I had any true friends. I know what it feels like and I know the dangers of putting people down. I never want anyone to feel the way I was made to feel.<P>When I got older and sort of came into my own, I was amazed at the people who wanted to be my friend all of a sudden. It almost made me mad. I was the same person.<P>All of my life I have tried to defend people that were attacked and made to feel small. It is not something that I try to do. I just care about people.<P>I remember being taught by some of my older relatives that you should 'Be careful what you say about someone. What if they believe you and never rise above it?'<P>I am one of the lucky ones. I had will power enough to prove to my step-father that he was wrong. Some people aren't so lucky.<P>Just be careful when you attack someone. You don't want to be the one responsible for making them not acheive all they could.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000083||Songman||07-29-2001||07:03 PM||||One more thing, Stage... and take this as a compliment... if she is your girlfriend, what the hell are you doing on here reading this stuff for anyway? I know I wouldn't be! heheh<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
